<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAAMBOU HALF YEAR EARNINGS UP A THIRD.</title>
<headline>SAAMBOU HALF YEAR EARNINGS UP A THIRD.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    15.9	    vs 12.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    2.6	     vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Attrib			 19.9	    vs 15.1</p>
<p>    Net interest income	142.7	   vs 118.7</p>
<p>    Other operating income   42.3	    vs 37.5</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 33.0	    vs 26.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			22.4	    vs 18.1</p>
<p>    Tax			    2.6	     vs 2.4</p>
<p>Div payable December 13</p>
<p>On register November 29</p>
<p>Full name: Saambou Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said advances grew 18.6 percent in the</p>
<p>period compared to 11.4 percent a year ago. Group assets now</p>
<p>exceed seven billion rand.</p>
<p>Saambou said it was confident that the current level of</p>
<p>growth in earnings would be maintained for the rest of the</p>
<p>financial year, given no signficant deterioration in the</p>
<p>economy.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
